    <item>
  <title>Austin Ed Fund awards $350,000 to boost Austin ISD educator projects (En español)</title>
  <link>https://www.austinisd.org/announcements/2026/09/09/austin-ed-fund-awards-350000-boost-austin-isd-educator-projects-en-espanol</link>
  <description>The&amp;nbsp;Austin Ed Fund&amp;nbsp;officially awarded $350,000 to support&amp;nbsp;48 innovative, educator-led projects&amp;nbsp;across Austin ISD through its 2026 Inspire the Future Grant program.&amp;nbsp;

The proposed initiatives centered on vital areas such as literacy, College &amp;amp; Career Readiness, and the educator experience.</description>
  <pubDate>Wed, 09 Sep 2026 15:50:39 -0500</pubDate>
    <dc:creator>jmaldonado</dc:creator>
    <guid isPermaLink="false">6383dd70-6957-4950-b314-7b17b42827e5</guid>
    </item>
<item>
  <title>Listen now! The Austin ISD official podcast for Sept. 8 (En español)</title>
  <link>https://www.austinisd.org/announcements/2026/09/08/listen-now-austin-isd-official-podcast-sept-8-en-espanol</link>
  <description>Boundary Realignment Update: The Board of Trustees will vote in October on Phase 1 of the boundary realignment for Marshall Middle School and Linder Elementary School. While the board votes this October, any approved boundary changes for Marshall and Linder will not take effect until the 2027–28 school year.&amp;nbsp;</description>
  <pubDate>Tue, 08 Sep 2026 12:55:54 -0500</pubDate>
    <dc:creator>jmaldonado</dc:creator>
    <guid isPermaLink="false">f3aa097d-a3e1-4845-8fcb-de01058bc9ef</guid>
    </item>
<item>
  <title>Austin ISD Official Podcast: Talking Academic Vision with Dr. Mary Ann Maxwell </title>
  <link>https://www.austinisd.org/announcements/2026/09/02/austin-isd-official-podcast-talking-academic-vision-dr-mary-ann-maxwell</link>
  <description>Welcome back to the Austin ISD Official Podcast. Here’s what's happening in our mid-week episode:&amp;nbsp;Academic Vision: Chief of Academics Dr. Mary Ann Maxwell sits down with Isadora Day to discuss campus-level academic progress, highlighting both the impressive strides students made last year and the ongoing work to shape the district's academic future.</description>
  <pubDate>Wed, 02 Sep 2026 16:43:29 -0500</pubDate>
    <dc:creator>jmaldonado</dc:creator>
    <guid isPermaLink="false">f355a85c-71aa-4d3e-ad74-6dc5b3a56a4d</guid>
    </item>
<item>
  <title>Listen now! The Austin ISD Official Podcast for Aug. 31 (En español)</title>
  <link>https://www.austinisd.org/announcements/2026/08/31/listen-now-austin-isd-official-podcast-aug-31-en-espanol</link>
  <description>Welcome back to the Austin ISD Official Podcast. Here’s what’s in this week’s episode: Academic Vision⁠: Chief of Academics Dr. Mary Ann Maxwell sits down with Isadora Day to discuss campus-level academic progress, highlighting both the impressive strides students made last year and the ongoing work to shape the district's academic future.</description>
  <pubDate>Mon, 31 Aug 2026 12:49:13 -0500</pubDate>
    <dc:creator>jmaldonado</dc:creator>
    <guid isPermaLink="false">8c6554d4-aca2-444a-b401-a233545c5c98</guid>
    </item>
<item>
  <title>Listen now! The Austin ISD Official Podcast (En español)</title>
  <link>https://www.austinisd.org/announcements/2026/08/24/listen-now-austin-isd-official-podcast-en-espanol</link>
  <description>In this episode, we dive into a major milestone for our district:&amp;nbsp;⁠Austin ISD has earned a 'B' accountability rating from the Texas Education Agency⁠. Superintendent Segura joins the show to discuss what this rating signifies for our schools, how campuses are growing, and why this is a clear sign that our entire system is moving in the right direction. </description>
  <pubDate>Mon, 24 Aug 2026 11:14:47 -0500</pubDate>
    <dc:creator>jmaldonado</dc:creator>
    <guid isPermaLink="false">daf08dcc-6451-4734-99d6-b7329abdb62c</guid>
    </item>
<item>
  <title>Austin ISD gains momentum, earns ‘B’ rating (En español)</title>
  <link>https://www.austinisd.org/announcements/2026/08/13/austin-isd-gains-momentum-earns-b-rating-en-espanol</link>
  <description>Dear Austin ISD Community,

Next week, nearly 70,000 students will walk through our doors—each bringing unique life experiences, strengths, and goals. We are ready and excited to welcome every student and ensure they grow academically throughout the year.

We are also starting the year with momentum: I’m proud to share that our district has officially earned a ‘B’ rating from the Texas Education Agency. This is our best rating as a district in four years.&amp;nbsp;</description>
  <pubDate>Thu, 13 Aug 2026 13:15:32 -0500</pubDate>
    <dc:creator>jmaldonado</dc:creator>
    <guid isPermaLink="false">468c3284-8a84-4313-b82a-77dd4f915786</guid>
    </item>
<item>
  <title>Austin ISD refines boundary realignment timeline amidst district updates (En español)</title>
  <link>https://www.austinisd.org/announcements/2026/08/11/austin-isd-refines-boundary-realignment-timeline-amidst-district-updates</link>
  <description>Throughout the summer Austin ISD has hosted virtual and in-person open houses to share boundary realignment ideas to help balance the number of students at campuses across the entire district. Through these meetings and the online comment card, the district has gathered valuable feedback from community members about the drafted “Oak” and “Elm” boundary scenarios.&amp;nbsp;</description>
  <pubDate>Tue, 11 Aug 2026 17:45:00 -0500</pubDate>
    <dc:creator>dgarcia</dc:creator>
    <guid isPermaLink="false">c31aadcf-a25e-42ae-8938-44cb0f0c2fa9</guid>
    </item>
<item>
  <title>Austin ISD 2026-27 Transportation Hubs and Feedback (En español)</title>
  <link>https://www.austinisd.org/announcements/2026/08/07/austin-isd-2026-27-transportation-hubs-and-feedback-en-espanol</link>
  <description>After careful consideration, we have decided to restore neighborhood-level bus stops for middle school students.&amp;nbsp;

With the closure of Paredes Middle school and other identified savings since the adoption of the 2026-27 budget, Austin ISD has decided to apply these savings to accommodate increased transportation costs related to adding back these stops.</description>
  <pubDate>Fri, 07 Aug 2026 17:53:14 -0500</pubDate>
    <dc:creator>dgarcia</dc:creator>
    <guid isPermaLink="false">60c12a28-dc75-4eb4-8301-0b654d779b64</guid>
    </item>
<item>
